        "date": "2026-11-11T17:53:37Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(app,ui): name the setup carry's turn, stop counting dialog time as a freeze\n\n#866: Setup2 held the part turned 90 degrees about X relative to Setup1,\na side-on turn the carried stock lattice refuses by design (lifting it\nis #874, after the field engine #637). The relative-turn composition is\nright; a test now pins that two setups turned alike carry.\n\n- The carry refusal names the turn between the setups (\"'Setup2' holds\n  the part turned X -90°, Y 0°, Z 0° from how 'Setup1' holds it\") and\n  CARRY_TURN_REFUSAL reads in plain words; the setup page says what to\n  do (choose \"Its own stock\", or hold the part as Setup1 does).\n- \"furniture\" leaves the Settings page's active-setup radio and the\n  Setups page footer.\n- The 35 s \"commands\" slow frame was the user browsing in the modal\n  file dialog: the dialog seam times every modal dialog and the frame\n  watch takes that time off the frame it happened in.\n\nFixes #872\nFixes #873\nRefs #866\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>\nClaude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01CUsqDAAAJyAPrC37zBzbbX",
